amination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course. Reading list 1. William Stallings and Lawrence Brown, Computer Security - Principles and Practice 4th edition, 2018 247 / 517 248 2. Mark S. Merkow and Jim Breithaupt, Information Security: Principles and Practices, 2nd edition, 2014. 2. Learning Outcomes Matrix The relationship between Course Learning Outcomes (CLO) (1-6) and Program/Student Learning Outcomes (SLO) (1-6) is shown in the following table: SLO',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,6),(9356,3053,'CLO1','Research a specific topic in the field. outcomes',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,1),(9357,3053,'CLO2','Design the model or system architecture of the application product',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,2),(9358,3053,'CLO3','Have a good preparation to develop and improve the product in the thesis.',NULL,'ATTITUDE',NULL,3),(9362,3055,'CLO1','Understand programming languages and applications, how applications work',NULL,'KNOWLEDGE',NULL,1),(9363,3055,'CLO2','Understand basic data structure and control flow of C programming language',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,2),(9364,3055,'CLO3','Able to write applications using C',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,3),(9625,3695,'CLO1','Understand programming languages and applications, outcomes how applications work',NULL,'KNOWLEDGE',NULL,1),(9626,3695,'CLO2','Understand basic data structure and control flow of C programming language',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,2),(9627,3695,'CLO3','Able to write applications using C',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,3),(9755,3730,'CLO1','Understand programming languages and applications, how applications work',NULL,'KNOWLEDGE',NULL,1),(9756,3730,'CLO2','Understand basic data structure and control flow of C programming language',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,2),(9757,3730,'CLO3','Able to write applications using C',NULL,'SKILL',NULL,3),(9758,3731,'CLO1','Understand the principles of computer architecture and the interfaces between its hardware and software components;',NULL,'KNOWLEDGE',NULL,1),(9759,3731,'CLO2','Understand computer arithmetic (both integer and