emic writing, and a research paper structure. Skill',NULL,NULL,NULL,1),(9783,3741,'CLO2','Discuss correct conventions for using sources, paraphrasing and summarizing, text structure and argumentation in common academic writing genres.',NULL,NULL,NULL,2),(9784,3741,'CLO3','CLO4 Ongoing assessment 30% (Participation 30 pts; Assignment Assignment Participation inclass assignment(s) 70 60%Pass 60%Pass 60%Pass pts) Part 1 Part 2 Midterm exam (20%) 60%Pass 60%Pass Part 1 Part 2 Final Examination (50%) 60%Pass 60%Pass Note: %Pass: Target that % of students having scores greater than 50 out of 100. 5. Rubrics: 5.1. Ongoing assessment - Attendance score (30 pts) - In-class assignment(s) (70 pts): discuss academic writing features (CLO1), sources citing (CLO2), paraphrasing and summaring (CLO2) 5.2. Midterm exam (written exam, closed-book exam, 60 minutes) Part 1: Identify non-academic features in an academic text and revise them. (30 pts) (CLO1) Part 2: Rewrite the following sentences or short texts (given in 2-3 sentences long with the reference list of the sources) in your own words without changing the meaning, and use correct in-text citations. (70 pts) (CLO2) 5.3. Final Exam (written exam, closed-book exam, 60 minutes) Part 1: Read a given research paper (around 700-1,000 words) and identify the extracts as part of the main component of a research paper (30 pts). (CLO2) Part 2: Write an analytical essay in 300-350 words (70 pts). (CLO3) 53 Revised date: April 23rd, 2026 Ho Chi Minh City, April 29th, 2026 Vice Dean of School of Languages Dr. Vu Hoa Ngan',NULL,NULL,NULL,3),(9785,3741,'CLO4','Display discipline, responsibilities, and ethical practices as an individual and a team member by attending class regularly and actively participating in class activities. Content The description of the contents should clearly indicate the weighting of the content and the level. Weight: lecture session (2 hours) Teaching levels: I (Introduce); T (Teach); U (Utilize) Topic Weight Level