s of this policy, detected using any AIwriting detectors, will lead to penalties. These penalties will only affect the idea development score, as specified below: Degree of similarity Description Below 15% Marked as it is. 16% - 25% The idea development score is deducted by 25%. 26% - 40% The idea development score is deducted by 50% Over 40% The idea development score is 0. Note: Part of the paper is marked as it is if no AI-generated text is detected. 51 Reading list Textbooks [1] Read, S. H. (2024). Academic writing skills for international students (2nd ed.). Bloomsbury Academic. [2] Hamp-Lyons, L., & Heasley, B. (2006). Study writing. Cambridge Unviersity Press. References [3] Bailey, S. (2018). Academic writing: A handbook for international students (5th ed.). Routledge. [4] Savage, A., & Shafiei, M. (2012). Effective academic writing 3 (2nd ed.). Oxford University Press. [5] Oshima, A., & Hogue, A. (2016). Writing academic English (5th ed.) Pearson. 2. Learning Outcomes Matrix (optional) 3. Planned learning activities and teaching methods Learning Week Topic CLO Assessments Resources activities Introduction to syllabus Class project [1] pp. 2-4 1 Appropriate writing 1 Lecture Midterm exam [2] pp. 19-20 style Final Exam Developing an academic Class project [1] pp. 4-10 Lecture, 2 writing style 1 Midterm exam Group work Final Exam Referencing and using Midterm exam [1] pp. 11-15 Lecture, 3 quotations 1 Class project Group work Final Exam Paraphrasing and Midterm exam [1] pp. 16-18 Lecture, 4 summarizing (1) 2 Class project Final Group work Exam Paraphrasing and Midterm exam [1] pp. 19-23 Lecture, 5 summarizing (2) 2 Class project Group work Final Exam Plagiarism and how to Midterm [2] pp. 140-144 avoid it Lecture, exam Class 6 2 Group work project Final Exam Plagiarism further Midterm exam [2] pp. 145-146 Lecture, 7 practice 2 Class project Group work Midterm review Final Exam 8 MIDTERM EXAM The structure of a Lecture, Class project Final [1] p. 89 research pap