having scores greater than 50 out of 100. 5.\",\"contentNote\":\"The description of the contents should clearly indicate the weighting of the content and the level. Weight: in the whole last semester Teaching levels: I (Introduce); T (Teach); U (Utilize)\"}','2026-09-09 10:12:39','2026-09-11 08:01:04','This course evaluates students obtained knowledges to complete the academic program.','Compulsory','Semester 8','English','Compulsory','Lecture, lesson, project, seminar.',NULL,'300 hours contact hours, self-','study hours) 300','Required number of credits recommended Special Study of the Field prerequisites for joining the course','Dissertations are industrial projects designed to ensure that students have mastered their subjects in the program. All projects are based on \"real projects\" provided by the industry to students to develop skills and apply knowledge gained from all courses throughout the program. Students will work independently to develop requirements, design, implement and provide solutions to business problems. Students can follow any appropriate process model, must self-manage the project, follow all appropriate project management techniques. The success of the project is largely determined by whether the student adequately solves the client\'s problem. Students will provide the final product with all artifacts that match the process model being used (e.g. project plan, technical requirements, system architecture, design documentation, test plan, source code and installed software products).','Multiple-choice questions, short-answer questions','Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory for examination the class sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of their class requirements participation. Questions and comments are strongly encouraged. Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course.',NULL,NULL,'IT058IU','Thesis',NULL,'CONFIRMED','Hồ sơ CTĐT Khóa 2026 - Khoa học máy tính - v7 - Tổng hợp.pdf','application/pdf','__AUDIT_RESET__3051','IMPORT_PDF',1),(3052,116,2,'v2.0','AUDIT2026','SUBMITTED',0,1,NULL,'2026-09-09 10:12:43',NULL,NULL,'{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"internalNotes\":\"\",\"personResponsible\":\"Dr. Le Hai Duong\",\"dateRevised\":\"2025-06-10\",\"creditPoints\":\"4 (ECTS: 6.18)\",\"lectureCredits\":\"3\",\"laboratoryCredits\":\"1\",\"workloadStudentResponsibility\":\"\",\"ploCodes\":[\"PLO1\",\"PLO2\",\"PLO3\",\"PLO4\",\"PLO5\",\"PLO6\"],\"cloPloMatrix\":{\"CLO1\":{\"PLO1\":\"x\",\"PLO2\":\"x\",\"PLO3\":\"x\"},\"CLO2\":{\"PLO2\":\"x\"},\"CLO3\":{\"PLO1\":\"x\"},\"CLO4\":{\"PLO1\":\"x\"},\"CLO5\":{\"PLO1\":\"x\"},\"CLO6\":{\"PLO1\":\"x\"}},\"topicDetails\":{\"0\":{\"clo\":\"CLO1\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"1\":{\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"2\":{\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"3\":{\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"4\":{\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment, Midterm\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"2\"},\"5\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"6\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"2\"},\"7\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"8\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"9\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"10\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5, CLO4\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment, Final examination\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"11\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"12\":{\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"1\"}},\"plannedActivities\":[{\"week\":1,\"topic\":\"Information security principles\",\"clo\":\"CLO1\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":2,\"topic\":\"Governance and risk management\",\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":3,\"topic\":\"Security architecture and design\",\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":4,\"topic\":\"Business continuity and disaster recovery planning\",\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":7,\"topic\":\"Operation security\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment, Midterm\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":10,\"topic\":\"Access control systems and methodology\",\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":11,\"topic\":\"Cryptography\",\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":12,\"topic\":\"Overview network and telecommunications security\",\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":13,\"topic\":\"Basic security infrastructures and routers\",\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":14,\"topic\":\"Firewalls\",\"clo\":\"CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":15,\"topic\":\"Intrusion detection systems and intrusion protection systems\",\"clo\":\"CLO4\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment, Final examination\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"}],\"assessmentCloMatrix\":{\"0\":{\"CLO1\":\"30.0\",\"CLO2\":\"20.0\",\"CLO3\":\"45.0\",\"CLO4\":\"25.0\",\"CLO5\":\"30.0\"},\"1\":{\"CLO1\":\"40.0\",\"CLO2\":\"75.0\",\"CLO3\":\"60.0\"}},\"readings\":[{\"title\":\"Computer Security - Principles and Practice 4th edition\",\"author\":\"William Stallings and Lawrence Brown\",\"publisher\":\"247 / 517 248\",\"year\":\"2018\",\"usageType\":\"REQUIRED\"},{\"title\":\"Information Security: Principles and Practices\",\"author\":\"Mark S. Merkow and Jim Breithaupt\",\"publisher\":\"2nd edition\",\"year\":\"2014\",\"usageType\":\"REQUIRED\"}],\"assessmentPassNote\":\"%Pass: Target that % of students having scores greater than 50 out of 100. 1. When calculating contact time, each contact hour is counted as a full hour because the organisation of the schedule, moving from room to room, and individual questions to lecturers after the class, all mean that about 60 minutes should be counted.↩︎ 5.\",\"contentNote\":\"\"}','2026-09-09 10:12:43','2026-09-11 08:01:05','The course will concentrate on security technologies that can be designation employed to safeguard and maintain a network. The course will also cover risk management, business continuity and recovery planning, operations security, access control systems, and software development security.','Compulsory',NULL,'English','Compulsory','Lecture, lesson, project, seminar.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Computer Networks recommended prerequisites for joining the course Course This course introduces students to information security principles, objectives cryptography systems (symmetric and public key encryptions), risk management, security architecture and design, business continuity operations security, access control systems, protecting TCP/IP network, firewalls, virtual private network, IPSec, software development security. Course CLO 1. Gain understanding of information security and the learning cryptography concepts including symmetric key encryption, hash outcomes function, message authentication code, public key encryption, digital signature and digital envelope; CLO 2. Apply the concepts of authentication and authorization in implementing secure systems and networks; CLO 3. Analyze and evaluate security risk and security design; 246 / 517 247 CLO 4. Understand and apply software development security; CLO 5. Apply security technologies in operations. Competency Course learning outcome level (CLO) Knowledge CLO1, CLO2, CLO4, CLO5 Skill CLO2, CLO3, CLO4, CLO6 Attitude Content The description of the contents should clearly indicate the weighting of the content and the level. Weight: lecture session (3 hours) Teaching levels: I (Introduce); T (Teach); U (Utilize) Topic Weigh Leve t l Information security principles 1 T Governance and risk management; 1 T,U Security architecture and design; 1 T Business continuity and disaster recovery 1 T,U planning; Operation security; 2 T,U Access control systems and methodology; 1 T Cryptography; 2 T,U Overview network and telecommunications 1 T,U security; Basic security infrastructures and routers; 1 T Firewalls 1 T,U Intrusion detection systems and intrusion 1 T protection systems Virtual private network and IPSec; 1 T Software Development security. 1 T,U Examination Multiple-choice questions, short-answer questions forms Study and Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory examination for the class sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of requirements their class participation. Questions and comments are strongly encouraged. Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course. Reading list 1. William Stallings and Lawrence Brown, Computer Security - Principles and Practice 4th edition, 2018 247 / 517 248 2. Mark S. Merkow and Jim Breithaupt, Information Security: Principles and Practices, 2nd edition, 2014. 2. Learning Outcomes Matrix The relationship between Course Learning Outcomes (CLO) (1-6) and Program/Student Learning Outcomes (SLO) (1-6) is shown in the following table: SLO CLO 1 2 3 4 5 6 1 X X X 2 X 3 X 4 X 5 X 6 X 3. Planned learning activities and teaching methods Week Topic CLO Assessments Learning Resour activities ces 1 Information security 1 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [1,2] principles Exercises, Lab 2 Governance and risk 3 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [2] management; Lab 3 Security architecture and 3 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [2] design; Lab 4 Business continuity and 3 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [2] disaster recovery planning; Lab 5,6 Operation security; 5 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [2] Lab 7 Access control systems and 2 Lecture, methodology; Lab Midterm exam 8, 9 Cryptography; 1 Quiz, Exam Lecture [1] 10 Overview network and 5 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [2] telecommunications; Lab 11 Basic security 5 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [2] infrastructures and routers; Lab 12 Firewalls 5 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [1,2] Exercises, 248 / 517 249 13 Intrusion detection systems 5 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [1,2] and intrusion protection Exercises, systems 14 Virtual private network and 5 Quiz, Exam Lecture, [1,2] IPSec; Lab 15 Software Development 4 Quiz, Exam Lecture [2] security. Final exam 4. Assessment plan Assessment Type CLO1 CLO2 CLO3 CLO4 CLO5 Exercises/ Quiz (20%) 30% 20% 45% 25% 30% Midterm examination 30% 80% 55% 10% (30%) Final examination (50%) 40% 75% 60% Note: %Pass: Target that % of students having scores greater than 50 out of 100. 1. When calculating contact time, each contact hour is counted as a full hour because the organisation of the schedule, moving from room to room, and individual questions to lecturers after the class, all mean that about 60 minutes should be counted.↩︎ 5. Rubrics (optional) 5.1. Grading checklist Grading checklist for Written Reports Student: HW/Assignment: ………………. …………………………….. Evaluator: ……………………… Date: ………………………………… Max. Score Comments