nt\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":6,\"topic\":\"2,\",\"clo\":\"CLO2, CLO4, CLO5\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":7,\"topic\":\"3, 5 HW Lectures and Quiz\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":8,\"topic\":\"3, 5 HW Lectures and Quiz\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment, Midterm\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":9,\"topic\":\"Maximum and Minimum Values, 2, 4 HW\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":10,\"topic\":\"2, 4 HW Lectures and Quiz\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":11,\"topic\":\"4, 5 HW Lectures and Quiz\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":12,\"topic\":\"Triple Integrals, Triple\",\"clo\":\"CLO2, CLO4\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":13,\"topic\":\"4, 5 HW Lectures and Quiz\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":14,\"topic\":\"2, 4, 5 HW Lectures and Quiz\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"},{\"week\":15,\"topic\":\"1, 2, 3, Exercises\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment, Final examination\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"\"}],\"assessmentCloMatrix\":{\"0\":{\"CLO1\":\"80.0\",\"CLO2\":\"80.0\",\"CLO3\":\"80.0\",\"CLO4\":\"80.0\",\"CLO5\":\"70.0\"},\"1\":{\"CLO1\":\"70.0\",\"CLO2\":\"70.0\",\"CLO3\":\"70.0\",\"CLO4\":\"70.0\",\"CLO5\":\"60.0\"},\"2\":{\"CLO1\":\"80.0\",\"CLO2\":\"70.0\",\"CLO3\":\"50.0\"},\"3\":{\"CLO1\":\"80.0\",\"CLO2\":\"50.0\"}},\"readings\":[{\"title\":\"Calculus, Thomson Learning\",\"author\":\"J. Stewart\",\"publisher\":\"7th edition\",\"year\":\"2012\",\"usageType\":\"REQUIRED\"}],\"assessmentPassNote\":\"\",\"contentNote\":\"The description of the contents should clearly indicate the weighting of the content and the level. Weight: lecture session (4 hours) Teaching levels: I (Introduce); T (Teach); U (Utilize)\"}','2026-09-15 04:10:27','2026-09-15 04:10:27','This course is a continuation of Calculus 1. Its aim is to equip student with basic concepts of sequence, series, vector functions, functions of several variables, multiple integrals and their applications','Compulsory','Semester 2','English','Compulsory','Lectures, assignments',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1. To provide students with the main ideas and techniques of calculus. These include sequences, series, functions of several variables, optimal problems, multiple integrals, vector calculus. 2. To introduce practical applications of these ideas and techniques, through practical examples taken from many areas of engineering, business, and life sciences. 3. To develop skills in mathematical modeling and problem solving, ability to think logically, and adapt these skills creatively to new situations Course learning Upon the successful completion of this course students will be able to: outcomes Course learning outcome (CLO) Competency level Knowledge CLO1. Have basic knowledge of series, functions of several variables, multiple integrals (Program outcomes: a) CLO2. Have basic knowledge of vector calculus (Program outcomes: a) Skill CLO3. Can compute partial derivatives, multiple integral (Program outcomes: a, j) CLO4. Can show the convergence of a sequence and a series and use power series to simplify computation. Can show the optimal problem using partial derivatives, can find the volume of an object in higher dimension by using the multiple integrals (Program outcomes: i, h) Attitude CLO5. Confident when dealing with partial derivatives, multiple integrals. Comfortable with using partial derivatives and multiple integrals in practical situations. (Program outcome: j, k) Content The description of the contents should clearly indicate the weighting of the content and the level. Weight: lecture session (4 hours) Teaching levels: I (Introduce); T (Teach); U (Utilize) Topic Weight Level Sequences and Convergence 1 I, T Series 1 I, T 1 T, U Tests for Convergence 1 T, U Power series 1 T, U Representations of Functions as Power series 1 T, U Taylor and Maclaurin series 62 1 I, T Vector Functions and Space Curves, Limit and continuity of vector functions 1 T, U Derivatives and Integrals of vector functions, Length of space curves 1 I,T Functions of Several Variables, Limits and Continuity 1 T, U Partial Derivatives, Tangent Plane and Linear Approximations 1 T, U Chain Rules, Directional Derivatives and Gradient 1 T, U Maximum and Minimum Values of Functions of two variables 1 T, U Lagrange Multipliers and Applications 1 I, T Double Integrals in Rectangles, Iterated Integrals 2 T,U Double, Triple Integrals in General regions and Applications Examination Written examination forms Study and Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory for the class examination sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of their class participation. Questions requirements and comments are strongly encouraged. Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course. Reading list J. Stewart, Calculus, Thomson Learning, 7th edition, 2012. 2.',NULL,'Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory for the class examination sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of their class participation. Questions requirements and comments are strongly encouraged. Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course.',NULL,NULL,'MA003IU','Calculus 2',NULL,'CONFIRMED','Hồ sơ CTĐT Khóa 2026 - Khoa học máy tính - v7 - Tổng hợp.pdf','application/pdf','CS-2021','IMPORT_PDF',0),(3744,122,1,'v1.0','CS2026','DRAFT',0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"internalNotes\":\"\",\"personResponsible\":\"Dr. Ta Quoc Bao Dr. Pham Hai Ha\",\"dateRevised\":\"2025-06-10\",\"creditPoints\":\"\",\"lectureCredits\":\"\",\"laboratoryCredits\":\"\",\"workloadStudentResponsibility\":\"\",\"ploCodes\":[\"PLO1\",\"PLO2\",\"PLO3\",\"PLO4\",\"PLO5\",\"PLO6\"],\"cloPloMatrix\":{},\"topicDetails\":{\"0\":{\"clo\":\"CLO1\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"1\",\"level\":\"I, T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"1\":{\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"2\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"2\":{\"clo\":\"CLO2\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"2\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"2\"},\"3\":{\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"4\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"4\"},\"4\":{\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"6\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"2\"},\"5\":{\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"4\",\"level\":\"I, T\",\"weight\":\"1\"},\"6\":{\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"2\"},\"7\":{\"clo\":\"CLO3\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"resources\":\"9\",\"level\":\"T, U\",\"weight\":\"2\"}},\"plannedActivities\":[{\"week\":1,\"topic\":\"Introduction to Probability\",\"clo\":\"CLO1\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"1\"},{\"week\":2,\"topic\":\"Counting techniques\",\"clo\":\"\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"2\"},{\"week\":3,\"topic\":\"Conditional probability and probability rules\",\"clo\":\"CLO2\",\"assessments\":\"Quiz / Assignment\",\"learningActivities\":\"Lecture\",\"resources\":\"2\"},{\"week\":7,\"topic\":\"Random variables and mathematical expectati