ical skills to identify social and environmental challenges, prototype solutions, and pitch viable sustainable business models, preparing them for an era of green transition and digital transformation.','Compulsory','Semester 7','English','Compulsory (CS, NE, CE) curriculum Elective (DS)','Lecture, lesson, project, seminar.','135','45 (lecture)','90','None','students with the ability to apply Design Thinking to create breakthrough solutions, build Lean Startup business models aligned with the UN 17 SDGs and ESG principles, and develop an Entrepreneurial Mindset to create positive value for the community. - Students will research, write, and present a sustainable business plan supported by financial modelling, marketing strategy, and a compelling pitch video. - CLO 1. Understand entrepreneurial processes, core innovation concepts, Lean Startup principles, and the 17 SDGs; identify the green economy context; demonstrate complex aspects of sustainable development (economic, environmental, social equity). - CLO 2. Apply new technology to boost business performance; proficiently apply Design Thinking and Lean Startup processes to identify problems, build sustainable business models, and Course learning deliver effective project presentations; outcomes - CLO 3. Manage marketing strategy and financial statements in an enterprise; develop a growth mindset, social responsibility, business ethics, and environmental awareness in problem- solving; Competency level Course learning outcome (CLO) Knowledge 1, 2, 3 Skill 1, 3 Attitude 3 The description of the contents should clearly indicate the weighting of the content and the level. Content Weight: lecture session (3 hours) Teaching levels: I (Introduce); T (Teach); U (Utilize) 27 Topic Weight Level Entrepreneurial Spirit & Sustainable 2 I, T Development; Innovation & Design Thinking; 4 I, T Lean Startup; 2 T,U Marketing Strategies & Sustainable Business 3 T, U Model; Finance, Accounting & Deal Structure 2 T, U The Art of Storytelling & Fundraising 2 T, U Examination forms Multiple-choice questions, short-answer questions Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory for the class sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of Study and their class participation. Questions and comments are strongly examination encouraged. requirements Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course. 1. Blank, S., & Dorf, B. The Startup Owner\'s Manual: The Step- By-Step Guide for Building a Great Company. K&S Ranch, 2020. (Textbook) 2. Adisa, A., Slobodan, P., & Roland, C. Sustainable Development Practice Reading list – Case Studies for Engineers and Scientists. Wiley, 2004 (References). 3. Scarborough, N. M., & Cornwall, J. R. Essentials of Entrepreneurship and Small Business Management (9th ed.). Pearson, 2019 (References). 2.','Multiple-choice questions, short-answer questions Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory for the class sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of Study and their class participation. Questions and comments are strongly examination encouraged. requirements Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course. 1. Blank, S., & Dorf, B. The Startup Owner\'s Manual: The Step- By-Step Guide for Building a Great Company. K&S Ranch, 2020. (Textbook) 2. Adisa, A., Slobodan, P., & Roland, C. Sustainable Development Practice',NULL,'{\"rubrics\":[{\"type\":\"ANALYTIC\",\"title\":\"Critical thinking value rubric for evaluating questions in exams\",\"scaleLabels\":[\"Level 1\",\"Level 2\",\"Level 3\",\"Level 4\"],\"criteria\":[{\"criterion\":\"Explanation of issues\",\"levels\":[\"Issue/problem to be considered critically is stated clearly and described comprehensively, delivering all relevant information necessary for full understanding.\",\"Issue/problem to be considered critically is stated, described, and clarified so that understanding is not serious