 forms Study and Attendance: A minimum attendance of 80 percent is compulsory examination for the class sessions. Students will be assessed on the basis of requirements their class participation. Questions and comments are strongly encouraged. Assignments/Examination: Students must have more than 50/100 points overall to pass this course. Reading list 1. William Stallings and Lawrence Brown, Computer Security - Principles and Practice 4th edition, 2018 247 / 517 248 2. Mark S. Merkow and Jim Breithaupt, Information Security: Principles and Practices, 2nd edition, 2014. 2. Learning Outcomes Matrix The relationship between Course Learning Outcomes (CLO) (1-6) and Program/Student Learning Outcomes (SLO) (1-6) is shown in the following table: SLO\", \"order_index\": 6, \"syllabus_id\": 3038, \"description_vn\": null, \"competency_level\": \"SKILL\"}], \"plo\": [{\"id\": 1, \"code\": \"PLO1\", \"category\": \"KNOWLEDGE\", \"is_active\": 1, \"created_at\": \"2026-06-04 19:37:27.000000\", \"program_id\": 1, \"description\": \"Analyze a complex computing problem and to apply principles of computing and other relevant disciplines to identify solutions.\", \"description_vn\": null, \"version_number\": 1}, {\"id\": 2, \"code\": \"PLO2\", \"category\": \"KNOWLEDGE\", \"is_active\": 1, \"created_at\": \"2026-06-04 19:37:27.000000\", \"program_id\": 1, \"description\": \"Design, implement, and evaluate a computing-based solution to meet a given set of computing requirements in the context of the program???s discipline.\", \"description_vn\": null, \"version_number\": 1}, {\"id\": 3, \"code\": \"PLO3\", \"category\": \"ATTITUDE\", \"is_active\": 1, \"created_at\": \"2026-06-04 19:37:27.000000\", \"program_id\": 1, \"description\": \"Communicate effectively in a variety of professional contexts.\", \"description_vn\": null, \"version_number\": 1}], \"book\": [{\"id\": 6799, \"url\": null, \"isbn\": null, \"year\": 2018, \"title\": \"Computer Security - Principles and Practice 4th e